# Own-wording spells of Valda's Spire of Secrets (2014 rules), part C.
HL = "\n\n**At Higher Levels.** "
TEXT = {
"Heart Of Darkness": ["1 mile, until dispelled, 1 hour cast. Raise up to 100 skeletons and zombies from graves in a mile. The heart holder gives general orders.",
 "1 mile, until dispelled, casting time 1 hour. You stab a black, ritually prepared human heart. Its ichor infects the land with necromantic energy, and up to one hundred piles of bones or corpses of Medium or Small humanoids within 1 mile rise as skeletons or zombies (the GM has the statistics). They dig out of graves, smash out of mausoleums and tear down cemetery gates.\n\nThe creature holding the heart can use its action to give one general command to all of them, such as destroy a town or hunt a creature, but only one command every 24 hours. Without a command they attack living creatures indiscriminately, except the holder and creatures it designates. Once ordered, they keep to the task until done. They are not under your direct control, so they do not count against limits on undead you command. They stay animated until the spell ends.\n\nThe spell ends if the heart is destroyed (AC 20, 10 hit points, immune to necrotic, poison and psychic damage) or hit by Dispel Magic cast as a 9th-level spell, or if every undead it created is destroyed. When it ends, all undead it raised collapse into heaps."],
"Hocuspocus": ["Cantrip, 30 ft, 1 minute. Create minor spooky effects: dimmed flames, eerie sounds, glowing orbs, a 10 ft chill or warmth, or rattling objects.",
 "30 ft, 1 minute. You conjure minor paranormal phenomena. Create one effect in range for 1 minute: all candles, torches and open flames darken and flicker; a quiet sound from a point you choose, such as whispers, insect drone or crying; up to four torch-sized glowing orbs that float around and give only a dim glow; chill or warm the air in a 10-foot cube by 10 degrees; or make small unattended objects rattle or rise an inch off the ground. If you cast it several times, up to three effects can be active at once, and you can dismiss one as an action."],
"Hollowing Curse": ["30 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. Dexterity save: 2d6 necrotic (half on a save) and a curse that lets you deal 1d6 each turn.",
 "30 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. Tendrils of black mist drain a creature you see. It makes a Dexterity save. On a failure it takes 2d6 necrotic damage and is cursed for up to a minute. On a success it takes half and is not cursed. While it is cursed you can use your action to deal 1d6 necrotic damage to it automatically. The curse ends early if you use your action for anything else, if the target leaves range, or if it has cover from you. Remove Curse also ends it." + HL + "Both damage amounts rise by 1d6 for each slot level above 1."],
"Hunger of the Earth": ["30 ft, Concentration, 1 hour. A Large or smaller creature is restrained and sinks into the ground, then suffocates.",
 "30 ft, Concentration, 1 hour. The earth opens beneath a Large or smaller creature on the ground and tries to swallow it. It makes a Strength save or is restrained, and on a failure it starts sinking. A restrained target, or a creature within 5 feet of it, can use an action to make a Strength check against your spell save DC to free it, and the target has Disadvantage on that check. The spell ends early if it is freed. At the end of the target's turn it sinks deeper: fully sunk after 2 rounds if Small or smaller, 3 if Medium, 4 if Large. Once fully sunk it begins to suffocate."],
"Ice Claw Prison": ["60 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. A Large ice claw (AC 18) slashes for 3d8 or imprisons a creature with 1d8 cold per turn.",
 "60 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. A Large clawed hand of razor-sharp ice appears in an unoccupied 10-foot square you see. It obeys you but cannot move from its place. It is an object with AC 18 and hit points equal to half your hit point maximum, immune to poison and psychic damage. At 0 hit points the spell ends. It does not fill its space. When you cast it, and as a Bonus Action on later turns, command it to do one of these:\n**Slash.** Melee spell attack against a target within 10 feet of the claw, dealing 3d8 slashing or cold damage (your choice).\n**Imprison.** The claw grabs a Large or smaller creature within 10 feet. It makes a Strength save against your spell save DC or is dragged into the claw's space and restrained. At the end of each of its turns it makes a Strength check against your spell save DC. On a success it escapes. On a failure it takes 1d8 cold damage. While it holds one creature the claw cannot imprison another. The claw can slash a creature it holds.\n**Release.** The claw lets an imprisoned target go." + HL + "The Slash and Imprison damage rises by 3d8 for each slot level above 3."],
"Icicle Javelin": ["60 ft. Ranged spell attack for 3d8 cold. A target next to a wall may be pinned (Speed 0 on a failed Strength save).",
 "60 ft. You fling a massive icicle at a target in range. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 3d8 cold damage. If it is next to a wall or similar large immobile object, it may be pinned to it. At the start of its next turn it makes a Strength save, and on a failure its Speed is 0 until the end of that turn." + HL + "The damage rises by 3d8 for each slot level above 1."],
"Identity Curse": ["Touch, until dispelled. Wisdom save or unconscious 1 hour and the target forgets its identity and personal memories.",
 "Touch, until dispelled. You touch a creature's temple and it forgets its own name. It makes a Wisdom save. On a failure it falls unconscious for 1 hour and is cursed to forget who it is. On waking it has lost all personal memories but keeps general knowledge, proficiencies and statistics. It does not realize it has class features or special abilities and so does not use them willingly. Left alone, it soon takes a new name and builds a new identity. Remove Curse cast with a 9th-level slot ends the curse, and the target regains all its memories."],
"Impressions of the Past": ["Self, Concentration, 1 minute. View your location at a chosen time up to 100 years ago. Share it at 8th level.",
 "Self, Concentration, 1 minute. You cast your senses back in time to perceive your current location as it was at an exact time you name, no more than 100 years ago, including events then. The view is dreamlike and shadowy, but you see detail and hear speech normally, and special senses such as darkvision work. You can look in any direction but cannot move or speak and cannot sense your present surroundings." + HL + "With an 8th-level slot or higher you can share the vision with one creature you touch. An unwilling target makes a Wisdom save to avoid it."],
"Indemnify": ["Bonus Action, 30 ft, Concentration, 1 hour. A marked target takes 1d8 radiant or necrotic whenever you lose hit points (Constitution save).",
 "30 ft, Concentration, 1 hour. You fling a drop of blood at a target you see, marking it for reckoning. It makes a Constitution save. On a failure it takes 1d8 radiant or necrotic damage (your choice) whenever you lose hit points for the duration. The spell ends early if the target starts its turn more than 60 feet from you."],
"Inevitable Boulder": ["60 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. An 8 ft boulder rolls 60 ft per turn after a target, hitting for 6d10 bludgeoning and pursuing for 24 hours.",
 "60 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. You conjure a Large, 8-foot-diameter boulder at a point in range that rolls after one creature you see. It has AC 18, 75 hit points, immunity to poison and psychic damage, and Resistance to nonmagical bludgeoning, piercing and slashing. At 0 hit points it vanishes and the spell ends. At the start of each of your turns it moves 60 feet toward its target. When it enters a creature's space, that creature makes a Dexterity save, taking 6d10 bludgeoning damage and being knocked prone if Large or smaller on a failure, or the same damage but no prone on a success. It crushes nonmagical objects smaller than itself. If it reaches the target it rolls over and continues its 60 feet, and it can roll over the target more than once. After the spell ends it keeps pursuing for up to 24 hours, and vanishes the moment it strikes its target."],
"Inexorable Sarcophagus": ["30 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. A sarcophagus grabs a Medium or smaller creature, which is buried alive after three failed saves.",
 "30 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. You toss a palm-sized sarcophagus at an empty point in range. It grows to full size at once and tries to ensnare a Medium or smaller creature within 5 feet with grimy gauze. The creature makes a Dexterity save or is restrained and pulled into the open sarcophagus. The gauze is an object with AC 10 and 100 hit points, vulnerable to slashing and fire, immune to psychic and poison. At 0 hit points the spell ends. The restrained creature makes another Dexterity save at the end of each of its turns. Three successes and it twists free and the spell ends. Three failures and the sarcophagus slams shut and sinks deep into the earth, the creature wrapped head to toe and incapacitated. The spell ends but the sarcophagus stays buried with 1 minute of air, after which the creature suffocates. A humanoid that dies inside rises 24 hours later as a mummy under your control, as with Create Undead, and you can command only one such mummy at a time. Later, you can use your action to make the sarcophagus rise to the surface, or shrink it back down while it is empty."],
"Instant Replay": ["Bonus Action, self, 1 minute. After your next missed attack, rewind and repeat it against the same target.",
 "Self, 1 minute. The next time you miss a creature with an attack before the spell ends, you can instantly reset to the moment before the attack and repeat it against the same target."],
"Intensify Gravity": ["100 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. A 50 ft radius cylinder doubles movement costs and object weight, gives ranged attacks Disadvantage and doubles falling damage.",
 "100 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. Gravity intensifies in a cylinder 50 feet in radius and 100 feet high centered on a point in range. Each creature there spends 2 feet of movement for each foot moved, including flying, jumping and climbing. With difficult terrain this slows movement to a quarter. A prone creature must succeed on a Strength check against your spell save DC to stand, and on a failure it cannot move on its turn. Objects, including worn and carried ones, weigh double, which can encumber creatures or make load-bearing spells like Levitate fail. Ranged weapon attacks into, out of or through the area have Disadvantage, and falling damage there is doubled."],
"Intrusive Thought": ["Reaction, 60 ft. When a creature attacks, Dashes, Dodges or Disengages, force it to take a different one of those actions (Wisdom save).",
 "Reaction, 60 ft. When a creature you see in range uses its action to Attack, Dash, Dodge or Disengage, you can try to twist its thinking. It makes a Wisdom save, and succeeds automatically if it cannot be charmed. On a failure it takes an action of your choice from those four instead of the one it intended."],
"Invisibility Purge": ["120 ft. Reveal and dispel magical invisibility within 120 ft, and suppress invisibility items for 1 minute.",
 "120 ft. You purge magical invisibility around you. Every creature, object, location or effect within 120 feet hidden by magical invisibility is revealed and the effect is dispelled. This includes innate magical abilities such as an imp's Invisibility, but it does not touch creatures on other planes such as the Ethereal Plane, nor reveal creatures that are naturally invisible. Items that grant magical invisibility, such as a Ring of Invisibility, are suppressed for 1 minute."],
"Jam Weapon": ["Reaction, 60 ft. A targeted firearm jams as it fires: the attack fails. More firearms with higher slots.",
 "Reaction, 60 ft. The firearm you target jams as it fires. The attack fails and the firearm is jammed. A jammed firearm cannot attack until a creature uses its action to clear it." + HL + "You can jam one extra firearm in range for each slot level above 2."],
"Jethro's Instant Reload": ["Touch, 1 hour. A ranged weapon reloads itself with ammunition teleported from you and ignores Loading.",
 "Touch, 1 hour. A ranged weapon you touch is enchanted to reload itself. If it has the Loading property, you ignore it for the duration. When its ammunition runs out, new ammunition teleports from your person into your hand or the weapon. If the weapon takes an action or longer to reload, it reloads at the end of your turn. If you do not carry enough ammunition, the spell ends."],
"Lashing Tendrils": ["Self, Concentration, 1 minute. Tendrils hit creatures within 5 ft when they arrive or start their turn there for 1d6 bludgeoning (Dexterity save for half).",
 "Self, Concentration, 1 minute. You sprout whipping tendrils that attack nearby creatures. When a creature comes within 5 feet of you or starts its turn there, it makes a Dexterity save, taking 1d6 bludgeoning damage on a failure or half on a success." + HL + "The damage rises by 1d6 for each slot level above 1, to a maximum of 6d6."],
"Legendary Libation": ["Cantrip, Bonus Action, self. Fill a container with a drink: it quenches thirst for 24 hours and gives Advantage on fear saves for 1 hour.",
 "Self. You speak a word of power and your container fills with a drink of your choice, which can be drunk as an action. It is delicious and satisfies thirst for 24 hours, and the drinker has Advantage on saves against being frightened for 1 hour. If not drunk within an hour, it becomes plain water. A creature gains the benefit of only one such libation per 24 hours."],
"Lightning Surge": ["Cantrip, 5 ft. Creatures within 5 ft make a Dexterity save or take 1d6 lightning.",
 "5 ft. You emit short lightning bolts in all directions. Every other creature within 5 feet of you makes a Dexterity save or takes 1d6 lightning damage.\n\nThe damage rises by 1d6 at level 5, 11 and 17."],
"Magic Daggers": ["Cantrip, 60 ft. Ranged spell attack with a force dagger for 1d6 piercing. More daggers at levels 5, 11 and 17.",
 "60 ft. You conjure a throwing dagger of force and flick it at a target you see. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 1d6 magical piercing damage. The dagger vanishes after the attack.\n\nYou conjure more daggers and make extra attacks: two at level 5, three at level 11, four at level 17. They can hit the same target or different ones, with a separate attack roll each."],
"Mandy's Enchanted Carriage": ["30 ft, 1 minute cast. Turn a vegetable into a Large carriage with two quasi-real horses, seating six, Speed 100 ft, lasting until midnight or 24 hours.",
 "30 ft, casting time 1 minute. You transform a vegetable into a Large magical carriage with reins and two quasi-real horses. It carries six: four inside and two on the coach seat. Creatures inside have full cover from external effects and see out through two windows of force. A creature on the seat can drive it, with Speed 100 feet, 10 miles an hour or 13 at a fast pace.\n\nWhere time passes normally, the spell lasts until the twelfth stroke of the next midnight. Elsewhere it lasts 24 hours. When it ends, occupants are ejected into adjacent spaces, the carriage shrinks back to a vegetable and the horses fade. The carriage and horses count as one object with AC 12 and 100 hit points, and the spell ends early at 0."],
"Mandy's Feral Follower": ["30 ft, 1 minute cast. Turn a Small or smaller beast (Int 3 or less) into a friendly commoner until midnight or 24 hours.",
 "30 ft, casting time 1 minute. After singing a song for the casting time, you touch a Small or smaller beast with Intelligence 3 or less. It becomes a humanoid with the statistics of a commoner and an appearance you choose. It is friendly to you and your allies, understands simple unskilled tasks and the languages you speak, but does not speak. It wears common clothes and has nothing else. In combat it rolls its own initiative and acts on its own turn as if dutifully employed by you.\n\nWhere time passes normally, the spell lasts until the twelfth stroke of the next midnight. Elsewhere it lasts 24 hours. It ends early if the target drops to 0 hit points or dies. It returns to the hit points it had before transforming, and excess damage from dropping to 0 carries over to its true form, which is not knocked unconscious unless that damage reduces it to 0." + HL + "You can transform one extra animal for each slot level above 4."],
"Mandy's Marvelous Dress": ["Touch, Concentration, 24 hours. A ball gown lets the wearer replace Charisma check rolls with 10 and makes attackers miss on a failed Wisdom save.",
 "Touch, Concentration, until midnight or 24 hours. A willing creature you touch is clothed in a fabulous, perfectly tailored ball gown with glittering jewelry. It can sit over the creature's clothing or armor, or replace its outfit. The wearer cannot remove the dress until the spell ends, and jewelry taken off vanishes. While it lasts, the wearer can replace the number it rolls on a Charisma check with a 10. If a creature that can see the wearer attacks it, the attacker makes a Wisdom save or misses. On a success the attacker is immune to this effect until the spell ends.\n\nWhere time passes normally, the spell lasts until the twelfth stroke of the next midnight. Elsewhere it lasts 24 hours. When it ends the dress vanishes in a puff of sparkles and the wearer's original outfit returns."],
"Mass Skirmish": ["30 ft, Concentration, 10 minutes. Any number of willing creatures gain +15 ft Speed, ignore nonmagical difficult terrain and provoke no opportunity attacks.",
 "30 ft, Concentration, 10 minutes. You boost the mobility of any number of willing creatures you see in range, so they move easily through enemy formations. For the duration each target's Speed rises by 15 feet, it ignores nonmagical difficult terrain, and it provokes no opportunity attacks."],
"Memorize": ["Touch. Remember a page of text exactly for a year, then Advantage on Intelligence checks to recall it.",
 "Touch. As you cast it, your eyes pass over the words on a page and commit them to memory. For the next year you remember every detail on that page exactly. After that you have Advantage on Intelligence checks to recall it. The material component is a page and a knotted length of silver string worth 10 gp, which the spell consumes."],
"Might of the Abyss": ["15 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. Three other creatures add 1d4 to weapon damage while within 15 ft of you.",
 "15 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. You channel stygian power into three creatures other than you in range. Whenever a target makes a weapon attack, it adds 1d4 to the damage roll. A target that moves more than 15 feet from you loses the effect until it is back in range." + HL + "The range rises by 5 feet and you can target one extra creature for each slot level above 1."],
"Minor Lifesteal": ["Cantrip, 60 ft. Constitution save or 1d4 necrotic, and you gain that many temporary hit points until a Long Rest.",
 "60 ft. You drain life from a hostile creature you see. It makes a Constitution save or takes 1d4 necrotic damage. You gain temporary hit points equal to the damage dealt, lasting until you finish a Long Rest. It has no effect on undead or constructs.\n\nThe damage rises by 1d4 at level 5, 11 and 17."],
"Moment to Think": ["Cantrip, Bonus Action, self. Stop time for others and take one extra Search or Use an Object action, or an Intelligence check to recall.",
 "Self. You briefly stop time for everyone but you. You can take one extra action and move around in your space while no time passes for others. That action can only be Search, Use an Object, or an Intelligence check to remember information about something. You cannot affect or damage any creature or object except things you wear or carry. An object that leaves your hand freezes in time."],
"Nondescript": ["Self, Concentration, 10 minutes. You seem ordinary: onlookers cannot recall details of your appearance.",
 "Self, Concentration, 10 minutes. You seem ordinary and forgettable without changing your appearance. Creatures that see you cannot recall specific details of how you look if asked whether they saw you or someone like you. Their memory of what you did and what happened is unaffected."],
}
